      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Higher doses mostly add peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, with little extra blood-pressure benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **10 mg PO daily**, the usual maximum.\n- **5 mg PO daily**, the usual starting dose. Some clinicians use 2.5 mg for frail patients.\n- **Another dose**, if 20 mg is intentional, for example because of a specialist recommendation or a specific protocol. If so, please confirm and I'll enter it with a note documenting that.\n\nIf the blood pressure isn't controlled on 10 mg, you could add a second agent instead, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide. I can enter that order too.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
